          "type": "RichText",
          "variant": "rich/story",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "Why it matters",
            "title": "Occupational back pain is a specification problem",
            "paragraphs": [
              "Lower back pain is the most common musculoskeletal complaint in office work, and most of it traces to chairs that support a posture nobody actually holds.",
              "The Anggun series was developed specifically around that finding: lightweight, responsive lumbar engineering aimed at shifts where the occupant moves constantly rather than settling into one position.",
              "Every mechanism decision above exists to keep support in contact with the spine while the occupant changes posture \u2014 not to hold them still."
            ],
            "aside": "All series are tested to BIFMA methods at our Klang facility before release to the line."
          }
        },
        {
